From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linyaDev <linyaDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:35:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make this CE match what Hardcore SK expects of it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pack does not run against untouched CE. It ships its own copy, trimmed and
edited, and its generated patches are written against that shape. One node
settles where such a fix belongs: the statBases/MarketValue its patches replace
on 46 ammo defs exists in neither upstream 1.6 nor 1.7 — only in the pack's copy.
These are HSK's edits inside CE, so they are made inside CE.

Five things the pack does to CE, done here:

  - 27 of the 28 files it edits: the diff upstream-1.6 -> the pack's copy, applied
    to the 1.7 file. The last one, Royalty's Buildings_Mechanoid, already carries
    the same content in 1.7.
  - all 222 ammo def files it disables, renamed to .xml.bak, which is its own way
    of switching CE content off: RimWorld reads only .xml. It has to be all of
    them — switching off the 15 that appeared in the log traded 61 errors for 63,
    because those files also declare the six generic ammo sets that dozens of
    CE's other sets reach through similarTo.
  - the 48 patch files it deletes outright, renamed the same way. Two of them
    mattered a lot: Weapons_Grenades.xml, whose smeltable=false against the pack's
    smeltProducts gave nine config errors, and RangedIndustrial_Biotech.xml, which
    gave four more.
  - the five def and patch files it adds to CE, copied in. Without them the
    deletions take content away: it drops upstream's 14.5x114mmSoviet.xml and
    ships its own 14.5x114mm.xml instead, and 35 of its patches target those defs.
  - the 106 textures it adds, copied in: 120mm tank and flak ammo, the
    night-vision apparel, and others its defs name but CE never shipped.

Two things are 1.7's own, reverted to how 1.6 behaved:

  - the weaponMoney 415~600 it adds to MercenarySniperBase, replaced by the node
    the pack actually patches. CE 1.6 does not touch that pawnkind at all; 1.7
    adds the value to the abstract base only, which is below the 950 the pack's
    cheapest sniper rifle costs, and leaves the pack's own Replace on the child
    defs without a target. The op here covers base and children, with a value
    above that threshold, and the pack overwrites it where it cares.
  - two fragment entries in the new Ammo_ChargedRockets.xml pointing at
    Bullet_164x284mmDemo_ASA and _ASB, which live in a file the pack disables.

Also 1.7's own: Patches/Core/ThingDefs_Misc/Weapons_Mech_Turrets.xml, a file CE
added in 1.7, points the mech mini-blaster at Bullet_6x22mmCharged and
AmmoSet_6x22mmCharged — ammo the pack switches off. The pack never saw the file,
so it could not have adjusted it. Repointed at 6x24mmCharged, the nearest live
charge calibre, which the pack keeps active and edits itself; otherwise that
turret has null for both projectile and ammo set.

One similarTo node is dropped, on AmmoSet_40x46mmOnlyEMP: it names the ammo set
from a file the pack disables. That set is new in 1.7, so the pack never saw it
and patches nothing about it — unlike the two neighbouring similarTo nodes, which
the pack removes itself and which therefore have to stay.

One redundancy removed: CE's own PatchOperationRemove of
Gun_Minigun/equippedStatOffsets. The pack removes exactly the same node, loads
after CE, and found nothing left to remove. The end state is identical — the node
is gone either way — and the pack's operation now lands.

One detail cost two rounds. CE moved the DLC patches a level deeper in 1.7 —
Biotech/Patches/X became Biotech/Patches/Biotech/X — so comparing by path skipped
those folders entirely, and that is where the last errors lived.

ModPatches is switched off in LoadFolders.xml, all 769 entries. The pack ships CE
without that folder at all, keeping the entries pointed at nothing; here the
folder exists, and with the full mod list it loads for whatever is installed and
brings references to content the pack disables — CE's Androids compat scenario
handed out Ammo_762x54mmR_FMJ, which lives in a file on the pack's .bak list. The
files stay; they simply are not attached, which is the same end state with a
five-line diff instead of 3819 deletions.

Also pins global.json to the SDK installed locally (10.0.401), since the branch
targets net10.0 while the file asked for 9.0.112.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
